<h1>array index</h1>
<p>
(definition)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
The location of an item in an <a href="array.html"><em>array</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Aggregate child</strong> (... is a part of or used in me.)<br>
<a href="oneBasedIndexing.html"><em>1-based indexing</em></a>, <a href="zeroBasedIndexing.html"><em>0-based indexing</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
In most programming languages, the first array index is 0 or 1, and indexes continue through the natural numbers.  The upper bound of an array is generally language and possibly system specific.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPR">PR</a></p>

